  "question": {
    "text": "A fair die is thrown <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> number of times. If the probability of always getting a number greater than the previous number is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>54</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is equal to <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total cases&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></math><br />Favourable cases&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></math><br />Required probability&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>54</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />by observation&nbsp;<math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> satisfies"
  }
